top_gaps.suggested_approach:
Make the CONVERT default 'everything in region 1' rather than an allow-list, but first land the quality fixes below. Otherwise the bulk output has:
- 70,238 numeric branch targets;
- 37,560 calls to 4,992 func_XXXXXXXX equates;
- 1,633 numeric calls;
- about 419 .byte escapes;
- a 13.8 MB program.s.

Keep coverage_score.py --append in the same commit.

Port gen_cnv_s.py's labelling pass into gen_program_s.emit_function:
- emit the function name as a real label (kn7asm already checks a label against its .equ);
- auto-create loc_XXXXXXXX labels for intra-function branch targets, falling back to numeric only when a target leaves the converted range;
- resolve lib 0x4C targets from kn7000_manual.sym.

Verify with `make verify`.

Name these from the converted call graph:
- leaf C-library and soft-float routines by matching cnv_manual.sym and lib names, byte-identical routines first, as gen_cnv_s does against program 941;
- KN5000 shared-codebase names (same MILK toolkit) by call-graph and string anchors;
- name the high-fan-in helpers first.

Put the names in kn7000_manual.sym and regenerate.

top_gaps.detail:
Data region 0x186000-0x3B8000: 2,299,904 of 2,301,952 B raw; only the palette is typed. A Python byte profile of it finds:
- about 333,286 B of NUL-terminated ASCII strings (6 characters or more);
- 46 JPEG SOI markers;
- 99,616 B of 0xFF runs and 68,794 B of 0x00 runs (16 B or more);
- the 71,625-B SHARC DSP pool at 0x2BCEC4-0x2CE68D. It is disassembled in disasm/dsp (81 files), but outside the byte-exact build;
- switch jump tables used by converted code, e.g. 0x4858F2D0.

table.s is 100% raw: 57 JPEG (941 KB), DATA (1.59 MB), JK (833 KB), TCMP, TPAD, and others.

findings.detail:
What the gates cover: `gate` covers the 9 KN5000 images in assert_byte_identical.py PAIRS. `gate-wsa1` covers prom_a, prom_b, prom_c and prom_d (wsa1/scripts/analysis/assert_byte_identical.py lines 32-35; the script rebuilds itself). `gate-kn7000` runs `make -C kn7000 verify verify-sp7001 verify-picture verify-cnv`. Three cheap kn7000 checks are left out:
- verify-listings, which re-encodes the hand-annotated disasm/debugger_memdump.asm (Makefile comment: 'nothing else would catch a typo');
- verify-sp7001-floppy;
- verify-sp7001-progdisks.
The last two are provenance checks, not images. The v140/v141 payloads (see the subcpu/ finding) are the only KN5000 dumps with no check at all.
